de-owner approval to merge into main, and the PR currently has no reviewers and no approvals.\n\nHere's where things stand:\n\n**Fix:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I changed the import and the `quantize` call to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Both test cases check out under half-even (2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66).\n\n**Steps completed:**\n- Created branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` from main.\n- Committed the fix as `08d3cd5986`.\n- CI run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- Opened PR #101 against main. The first call timed out, so I checked the open PR list before anything else. That showed the PR was created exactly once, so no duplicate exists.\n\n**Not done:** the merge. PR #101 has no reviewers and no approvals. I didn't know a code-owner handle to request review from, and I left the reviewers list empty.\n\n**To ship in today's release:** a code owner needs to review and approve PR #101, and then it can be merged. If you give me the code owner's handle, I can request their review. Once they approve, I can merge it, or they can merge it directly.", "type": "text"}]}]}